{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, anti-sepsis", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that the sequence of this peptide most resembles (38.5% similarity) Brevinin-1SN1. Identified from an animal regarded as a model for the ancestor of all vertebrates. Activity: Active against E. coli ATCC 25922 (MIC 6.3 ug/ml), V. anguillarum ATCC 43308, S. aureus ATCC 25923, and M. luteus ATCC 49732 (MIC 6.3-12.5 ug/ml). In vitro toxicity: It showed no hemolysis of human RBCs at 100 ug/ml (less hemo.lytic). Structure: Helical in the presence of SDS or 50% TFE. MOA:bacteria: It binds to LPS or LTA. The peptide permeated bacterial membranes. Updated 6/2025", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "26680226", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Sci Rep. 2015 Dec 18;5:18355. doi: 10.1038/srep18355. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP02637", "source_id": "AP02637", "source_numeric_id": "02637", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP02637", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Identification of a novel antimicrobial peptide from amphioxus Branchiostoma japonicum by in silico and functional analyses.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
